{"parentUuid":"d7a618f3-9736-499b-aa94-dc0e2b265ac5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"42080e8f-77b8-445b-960f-3f365e46f9e1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Review our stateful coordination class for alarm-handling bugs and tell me what to change.\n```ts\nexport class Room extends DurableObject {\n  async fetch(request: Request) {\n    const count = (await this.ctx.storage.get<number>(\"count\")) ?? 0;\n    await this.ctx.storage.put(\"count\", count + 1);\n    setTimeout(() => this.flush(), 60 * 60 * 1000);\n    return new Response(String(count + 1));\n  }\n  async alarm() {\n    await this.flush();\n  }\n  async flush() {\n    const pending = await this.ctx.storage.get<string[]>(\"pending\");\n    await fetch(\"https://example.com/sink\", { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify(pending) });\n  }\n}\n```"},"uuid":"a2bf9fb0-bc2b-4835-9473-3412c1a1a75f","timestamp":"2026-11-09T15:27:49.709Z","permissionMode":"auto","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":1},"sessionId":"5f91e8f6-3987-49cc-9b2a-5f72af9a4925","version":"2.1.319"}
{"parentUuid":"b628691a-d91f-491a-80f1-9fc64faceee4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsbBdCd3KC8tkrL7JD4U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6784,"cache_read_input_tokens":9130,"output_tokens":2959,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1991},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6784,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2959,"cache_read_input_tokens":9130,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6784},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null}},"thinkingDurationMs":9980,"thinkingDisplay":"omitted","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"b393458c-fc2c-45dc-8f37-8d3ceea9af98","timestamp":"2026-11-09T15:28:01.989Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionId":"5f91e8f6-3987-49cc-9b2a-5f72af9a4925","version":"2.1.319"}
{"parentUuid":"b393458c-fc2c-45dc-8f37-8d3ceea9af98","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsbBdCd3KC8tkrL7JD4U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The class has four alarm-handling bugs. The first two mean the flush never runs as intended.\n\n1. **The alarm is never scheduled.** Nothing calls `ctx.storage.setAlarm()`, so `alarm()` never fires. The only trigger is `setTimeout`.\n\n2. **`setTimeout` is not durable.** The timer lives in memory. If the object is evicted or restarted before 60 minutes pass, the flush is lost. Each request also adds another timer, so one window can flush many times.\n\n3. **`flush()` reads a key nothing writes.** `fetch` writes `\"count\"`, but `flush` reads `\"pending\"`. `pending` is always `null`, so the sink receives the body `null`.\n\n4. **`flush()` never clears what it sent and ignores failures.** It does not check `res.ok`, so a 500 from the sink counts as success. It also never deletes `pending` after sending, so the same data is sent again on every run.\n\nFix: schedule one alarm per window, store the data it will flush under a key that `fetch` writes, treat non-2xx as an error so the alarm retries, and delete the data only after the sink accepts it.\n\n```ts\nexport class Room extends DurableObject {\n  async fetch(request: Request) {\n    const pending = (await this.ctx.storage.get<string[]>(\"pending\")) ?? [];\n    pending.push(new Date().toISOString());\n    await this.ctx.storage.put(\"pending\", pending);\n\n    if ((await this.ctx.storage.getAlarm()) === null) {\n      await this.ctx.storage.setAlarm(Date.now() + 60 * 60 * 1000);\n    }\n    return new Response(String(pending.length));\n  }\n\n  async alarm() {\n    await this.flush();\n  }\n\n  private async flush() {\n    const batch = await this.ctx.storage.get<string[]>(\"pending\");\n    if (!batch || batch.length === 0) return;\n\n    const res = await fetch(\"https://example.com/sink\", {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" },\n      body: JSON.stringify(batch),\n    });\n    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`sink returned ${res.status}`);\n\n    await this.ctx.storage.delete(\"pending\");\n  }\n}\n```\n\nTwo points about this version:\n\n- Each `alarm()` run calls `setAlarm` only when none is set, and the runtime clears the alarm before calling `alarm()`, so the next request schedules a new window.\n- The outbound `fetch` does not block other events, so a request can append to `pending` while the sink call is in flight. The `delete` then drops that request's entry. To avoid this, move the batch to its own key before sending (`put(\"inflight\", batch)` and `delete(\"pending\")`), delete `inflight` after success, and on failure merge `inflight` back into `pending` before rethrowing. The sink must also tolerate a resend after a timeout, since a retry can post the same batch twice."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6784,"cache_read_input_tokens":9130,"output_tokens":2959,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1991},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6784,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2959,"cache_read_input_tokens":9130,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6784},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestedModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"b53baf36-e49f-4d01-8024-3789a328130c","timestamp":"2026-11-09T15:28:05.757Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionId":"5f91e8f6-3987-49cc-9b2a-5f72af9a4925","version":"2.1.319"}
